elaine: Quick heads-up — opening a docs PR to unify streaming examples across py/ts/go. PR #4728. Goal: show the new streaming iterator + backoff/retry pattern + cursor-based pagination in one mini-cheatsheet. Need quick review on snippet clarity and link targets.

sam: Nice. Can you call out the breaking change? i.e., old `stream()` -> new `stream_iter()` and the `has_more` cursor semantics.

elaine: Yup — I added a short note at top. Also replaced the old `on_data` callback example with an async iterator example. Example updated for three languages.

rohit: Quick skim — Python snippet looks good but the retry loop may double-await in some edge cases. Suggest this pattern:```
# python streaming + retries (recommended)
from redwood import Client, StreamError

client = Client()

async def stream_with_retries(prompt):
    backoff = 0.5
    max_backoff = 4
    for attempt in range(5):
        try:
            async for chunk in client.stream_iter(model="rwd-large", prompt=prompt):
                yield chunk
            return
        except StreamError:
            await asyncio.sleep(backoff)
            backoff = min(max_backoff, backoff * 2)
            continue
    raise RuntimeError("stream failed after retries")
```

maria: TS snippet should show both promise + async-iterator flavors. For Node we prefer `for await (const part of client.streamIter(...))` rather than callbacks. Also add note about `signal` for aborting. Example I wrote:```
// typescript streaming + abort
const client = new RedwoodClient();
const ac = new AbortController();

try {
  for await (const chunk of client.streamIter({ model: 'rwd-small', prompt })) {
    process.stdout.write(chunk.text);
  }
} catch (err) {
  // apply retries externally, or use controller.abort()
}
```

elaine: Good. Also included a short Go example that shows the cursor/pagination approach for long outputs (chunked continuation). I kept it tiny so it doesn't bloat the page.```
// go streaming pseudo-example
stream, err := client.StreamIter(ctx, "rwd-small", prompt)
if err != nil { log.Fatal(err) }
for stream.Next() {
    part := stream.Value()
    fmt.Print(part.Text)
}
if err := stream.Err(); err != nil { /* handle */ }
```

rohit: Sounds solid. One more ask: add an explicit snippet showing cursor-based resume when connection drops (use `cursor_id`), otherwise folks will miss it.

elaine: Done — added a tiny python snippet that resumes with `cursor_id` plus a note about TTL on cursors.

sam: Link fixes: update the streaming reference link to /docs/api/streaming-v2 and the pagination guide to /docs/guides/pagination. Also add an anchor to the SDK migration note.

elaine: Links updated. I also added a short checklist in the PR description: 1) confirm no stale import names, 2) ensure code blocks are runnable (no fake names), 3) run smoke examples in CI, 4) add redirects from old streaming page.

maria: CI smoke run passed for py + ts, go needs a tiny shim fix (client.StreamIter signature). I'll push a quick patch to the PR.

